  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">PERFORMANCE-BASED PARTNERSHIP SCHEME FOCUSING ON QUALITY PROGRAMMING, UNDERSTANDING CHANGE AND RESULTS FOR POOR HOUSEHOLDS AND COMMUNITIES</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Improved capacity of vulnerable households to positively respond to climate shocks (floods) and reduce the need for negative coping strategies via distributions of water purification sachets..  OVERALL COUNTRY PROG: Outcome 1.  SPECIFIC OUTCOME: This was an acute humanitarian crisis response intervention, targetting vulnerable households, particularly female headed households and those households with young children, elderly and disabled individuals. The programme was designed to be gender responsive as the restoration of WASH facilities not only met the needs of the affected population, while assisting in the protection of women and girls from SGBV</narrative>
  </description>
